# OTA after each request

After completing a user request that changes app JS/TS, assets, or app config that ships via Expo Updates:

1. Publish OTA to **both** `production` and `development` channels (user may open either build):
   ```
   npx eas-cli@latest update --channel production --environment production --message "<short summary>" --non-interactive
   npx eas-cli@latest update --channel development --environment production --message "<short summary>" --non-interactive
   ```
2. Briefly tell the user the dashboard links when done.
3. Skip OTA only for pure docs/rules, questions with no code changes, or when the user explicitly says not to publish.
4. Native-only changes that need a new binary still need `eas build` — say so and still publish OTA for the JS part if any.
5. Do **not** auto-`reloadAsync` on launch/AppState — it crashed users. Fetch in background and let the banner / manual install apply. Never add top-level imports of new native modules in code paths loaded at app start (lazy-import instead) unless a new native binary is shipped.
